---
// Pearl › 06 — The Exception: an aside (label, italic quote, short accent rule) beside two
// italic paragraphs. Set in Google Sans Code italic on purpose (DESIGN.md › Google Sans Code).
// 80px band padding instead of 120. Figma's 32 line height on the paragraphs uses the
// pearl-quote token's 30.
import Section from './Section.astro';
---

<Section tone="white" width="wide" compact labelledby="exception-title">
  <div class="layout">
    <aside class="aside">
      <h2 class="text-label-s label" id="exception-title">one exception, early in the build</h2>
      <p class="text-pearl-quote quote">A quiet lesson about skipping the queue.</p>
      <span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </aside>

    <div class="body text-pearl-quote text-body-l-mobile">
      <p>
        Before Pearl covered dark mode, the client asked for two screens ahead of schedule — Home
        Screen and My Plan. Home Screen made sense early; it settled UI direction everyone needed
        to agree on. My Plan didn't need to jump the queue, but it did anyway.
      </p>
      <p>
        The cost showed up later. When dark mode became urgent for the dev team, both screens had
        to be retrofitted component by component, because they'd never been built against the
        system in the first place. It was avoidable, and it's the clearest argument I have for
        pushing back harder next time a “quick” UI request tries to skip the system.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  .layout {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-64);
  }

  /* Figma gap 18, snapped to 16. Label and quote wrap at the 220 width, as in Figma. */
  .aside {
    flex: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    width: 220px;
  }

  .label {
    max-width: 120px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* The 16/24 pearl-quote size. */
  .quote {
    max-width: 200px;
    font-size: var(--body-l-size);
    line-height: var(--body-l-line);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .rule {
    width: 52px;
    height: 2px;
    background-color: var(--pearl-accent-line);
  }

  /* Figma gap 22, snapped to 24. */
  .body {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Tablet and mobile: the aside sits above the paragraphs. */
  @media (max-width: 1199px) {
    .layout {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-40);
    }
  }

  /* Mobile: 24 between the headline and the text, the same in every section (user). */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .layout {
      gap: var(--space-24);
    }
  }
</style>
